test(decision): lock the BLOCK invariant across every category

Property test over category × severity × source × confidence × tier × --fail-on
— 20,400 evidence shapes — asserting that no combination reaches BLOCK without
a corroborating signal, and that no MEDIUM-band finding reaches BLOCK without an
INDEPENDENT one. Severity is a constant chosen by the scanner; it must never be
sufficient on its own.

The category list is explicit rather than derived: bringing a new category under
this invariant should be a conscious act, not something that happens silently
when someone adds a string elsewhere.

Four companion guards, each covering a way this change could be wrong rather
than merely incomplete:

  TestConfirmedFindingsStillBlock       the gate is still reachable, once per
                                        confirmation mechanism — a gate nobody
                                        can trip is a removal, not a fix
  TestEveryBlockNamesItsCorroboration   no BLOCK ships an empty justification
  TestDecisionIsDeterministic           200 iterations, verdict + reason +
                                        score + signal ORDER stable
  TestLegacyPolicyIgnoresCorroboration  --enforce-confidence=false still
                                        restores the severity-only mapping

Full suite: 39 packages ok, 0 failures, stable at -count=2.

